If a clinician conducts a follow-up with a patient then the clinician should review a patient-perspective with the patient and should review a patient-goal with the patient and should determine a continued-opioid-goal-attainment for the patient and should assess a sustained-pain-improvement for the patient and should assess a sustained-function-improvement for the patient and should assess a common-opioid-adverse-event for the patient and should assess a serious-opioid-adverse-event for the patient and should assess a serious-opioid-adverse-event-warning-sign for the patient and should assess an opioid-use-disorder-sign for the patient.
